{"symbol":"MGT.WA","area":"poland","updated":"2026-11-09T19:53:19Z","info":{"address1":"Cechowa 6/8","city":"Bielsko-Biala","zip":"43-300","country":"Poland","phone":"48 33 475 2008","fax":"48 33 475 2009","website":"https://mangata.com.pl","industry":"Metal Fabrication","industryKey":"metal-fabrication","industryDisp":"Metal Fabrication","sector":"Industrials","sectorKey":"industrials","sectorDisp":"Industrials","longBusinessSummary":"Mangata Holding S.A. produces and sells fittings, castings, elements, fasteners, and components in Poland, Germany, Finland, the Czech Republic, Switzerland, the rest of the European Union, the United States, and internationally. The company offers forgings, exhaust systems, and metal components; and car parts, mechanical parts for vacuum pumps, servo drive parts, parts for construction and agricultural machinery, and hydraulic units. It also provides stop, bellow, check, butterfly, ball, and gate valves; and strainers, backflow preventers, and rubber expansion joints. In addition, the company offers advanced engineering services for the implementation of the research and development of industrial valves. Further, it provides bolts, nuts, washers, rivets, and other fasteners. The company serves the automotive, mining, construction, gas and power, agriculture, heating distribution and technology, ventilation and air conditioning, water supply and sewage system, shipbuilding, industrial valve, control of valves, railway, and machine industries. It exports its products to approximately 70 countries, including the Netherlands, Italy, Sweden, France, Egypt, Indonesia, Brazil, China, the United Arab Emirates, Saudi Arabia, and South Africa. The company was formerly known as ZETKAMA Spólka Akcyjna and changed its name to Mangata Holding S.A. in September 2016. The company was founded in 1946 and is headquartered in Bielsko-Biala, Poland. Mangata Holding S.A. operates as a subsidiary of Capital MBO Spolka z ograniczona odpowiedzialnoscia.","f